---
description: Use when a task references a Figma URL, a design handoff, exported Figma assets, Figma design-system mappings, or Code Connect. Do not use for ordinary Nuxt implementation without Figma context.
alwaysApply: false
---

- Use the official provider Figma skills rather than copied or forked vendor
  skills. For design-to-code, load `figma-design-to-code` before requesting
  design context; treat generated reference code as input to adapt to Nuxt and
  this repository, never as code to paste verbatim.
- Require a node-specific Figma URL for implementation work. Start read-only:
  request design context, inspect existing components and tokens, then map the
  result to this project's Nuxt, UnoCSS, native CSS, SSR, SEO, and CWV patterns.
- The default project handoff is [DeployLab — Copy / root node 0:1](https://www.figma.com/design/0dto2dTdI7m3yyEelxxgDz/DeployLab--Copy-?node-id=0-1&p=f&m=dev).
  It is a read-only source unless the user names an exact Figma write operation.
- Prefer existing project components and tokens. Preserve semantic HTML and
  rendering strategy; do not add `ClientOnly`, client-only design libraries,
  external scripts, or layout shifts merely to match a canvas.
- Download exported Figma assets promptly and commit exact source assets only
  when their licence and repository need are clear; temporary MCP asset URLs
  are not production asset URLs. Verify changed UI in a real local browser.
- Figma reads are limited to the user-supplied design target. Any Figma write,
  delete, publish, capture, or code-to-canvas synchronisation requires the
  user's explicit approval for that file and operation, and must report the
  affected node IDs.
- Keep Code Connect and `@figma/code-connect` out of scope until this repository
  has stable reusable components and agreed Figma component mappings; at that
  point, use its official CLI and environment-only credentials.
